     The ttoouuppppeerr() and ttoouuppppeerr__ll() functions convert a lower-case letter to
     the corresponding upper-case letter.  The argument must be representable
     as an _u_n_s_i_g_n_e_d _c_h_a_r or the value of EOF.

     The ttoouuppppeerr__ll() function takes an explicit locale argument, whereas the
     ttoouuppppeerr() function uses the current global or per-thread locale.

